Author: Angel Mendez

How to run: 

sudo python3.lab7.py target domain(google.com) #(Max # of hops)

Questions: 

1) Besides TCP, what other protocols can be used for a traceroute tool?

Answer: Tracerout also can use UDP and ICMP while traditional linux uses UDP packets and windows tracert uses ICMP echo requests


2) When traversing to a website, does the path remain constant every time?

Answer: No, the path can change between each attmept and the internet routing can change depending on congestion

3) If a packet dies before reaching the target website, what type of
   packet is returned?

Answer: An ICMP time exceeded packet is returned when the time to live reaches 0 before reaching the destination 

4) Can the whois command be used to discover the owner of an AS number?

Answer: Yes, Whois can show info about the organization that owns an autonomous system number 

